repository_workspace_protocol
  record_type "meta_recipe"
  issue "1138"
  topic "repository_workspace"
  title "One repository protocol for SWE-bench, the coding ladder and self-coding"
  summary "One protocol for SWE-bench, the #848 ladder and self-coding. Grounded by tests/unit/specification/repository_workspace_protocol.rs against the live source, so the step order is data: adding a step is an edit to this document, not an edit to Rust."
  generalization "To run any repository task, instantiate the six ordered steps below against a RepositoryWorkspace: materialise the tree at an exact commit, resolve what the requirement names, read those bytes, apply the change, run the named tests on a declared backend, and emit the unified diff. Every step records an execution record before the next step is planned, so a step that did not run leaves its need planned rather than satisfied."
repository_step_clone
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "1"
  id "clone"
  title "Materialise the origin at the exact base commit"
  detail "Materialise the origin at the exact base commit. A branch name is refused: a task defined against a moving reference is not reproducible."
  precondition "task carries an origin and a 40-character base commit"
  postcondition "the checked-out HEAD equals base_commit"
  source_file "src/repository_workspace/clone.rs"
repository_step_locate
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "2"
  id "locate"
  title "Resolve the files the requirement names"
  detail "Resolve the files the requirement names: census for Rust trees, literal and path occurrence otherwise. The requirement arrives as the need's subject in the need's own language, so five held-out languages are one code path. Ambiguity resolves to nothing and the candidates are reported."
  precondition "clone postcondition observed"
  postcondition "at least one Location, or an explicit unresolved need naming the candidates"
  source_file "src/repository_workspace/locate.rs"
repository_step_read
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "3"
  id "read"
  title "Read the located bytes and snapshot them"
  detail "Read every located file and retain its bytes as the baseline, so the diff at the end is computed from what the protocol actually observed rather than from a second version-control call."
  precondition "at least one Location was resolved"
  postcondition "every located path has baseline bytes"
  source_file "src/repository_workspace/mod.rs"
repository_step_edit
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "4"
  id "edit"
  title "Apply the change and observe the bytes written"
  detail "Apply the change and read the file back, so the edit is an observation rather than an intention. A write that cannot be read back is a failure of the step, not of the answer."
  precondition "baseline bytes exist for the target path"
  postcondition "one execution record per written file, carrying the digest of the bytes read back"
  source_file "src/repository_workspace/edit.rs"
repository_step_verify
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "5"
  id "verify"
  title "Run the named tests on a declared backend"
  detail "Run the named tests on the declared execution backend. A missing interpreter, compiler or container is a missing prerequisite handed to the recovery path: it is never a pass and never a silent skip, and a timeout is reported with both the deadline and the elapsed time."
  precondition "the edit postcondition was observed"
  postcondition "one execution record naming the passed and failed test names, or a missing-prerequisite report"
  source_file "src/repository_workspace/verify.rs"
repository_step_diff
  record_type "meta_step"
  order "6"
  id "diff"
  title "Emit the unified diff and prove it applies"
  detail "Emit the unified diff between the base commit and the current tree. A diff that does not apply cleanly to a second clone at the same base commit is refused before it is offered as an answer."
  precondition "the verify step produced an execution record"
  postcondition "a unified diff that round-trips through a clean apply at base_commit"
  source_file "src/repository_workspace/diff.rs"
